 "labels": [
  {
   "language": "en",
   "status": "official",
   "text": "Section 55(b)(1)(A): the taxable excess above which the 28 percent AMT rate applies (\"$175,000\", 2012 base year; indexed after 2012 under section 55(d)(3)). Married individuals filing separately use 50 percent of the amount (section 55(b)(1)(C)); the parameter is the amount for all other taxpayers. Years between the anchored rows are NOT pinned in this package (no Revenue Procedure text for them is in us.irc.inflation_adjustments): evaluation returns MISSING_PARAMETER_VALUE there instead of a fabricated indexed figure (TECH-GAPS, income-individual stage 2 AMT)."
  }
 ],
